	<h1>Getting started</h1>
	<norn-rich-text>
		<p id="overview">Overview: a level 3 heading first, so it has no parent and sits at the top.</p>
		<p>The contents sit in a column beside the page and follow it as it scrolls. The link for the section in view takes the accent, so a reader can tell where they are.</p>
		<p id="setup">Setup: a level 2 heading.</p>
		<p>Each link points to a heading in this same page, so selecting one scrolls to it. Keep the headings short, and let the list name the sections in the order they appear.</p>
		<p id="tokens">Design tokens: a level 4 heading under a level 2, so it nests one list down with no empty list between.</p>
		<p>The contents sit in a column beside the page and follow it as it scrolls. The link for the section in view takes the accent, so a reader can tell where they are.</p>
		<p id="usage">Usage: a level 2 heading.</p>
		<p>Each link points to a heading in this same page, so selecting one scrolls to it. Keep the headings short, and let the list name the sections in the order they appear.</p>
	</norn-rich-text>
</norn-sidebar-layout>
